  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14233881/assets/553af60aa28cbdd7565259eacc167187bc9c63a5b30cd78a6c14a3c43603fca2.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?",
  "worked_solution": "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(5,3).$ So, our actual value is $y=3.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=5$ has the $y$-coordinate $5.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14233881/assets/c558c80b7056b794534146d3b99f399c3084806758f78bd6eddb39e8c89248e9.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =3-5 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
